From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:35:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: fail a buffer map whose staging buffer was refused

The staging buffer of a write-only buffer map is allocated from the
stream uploader, or created outright, and the code went on to use the
resource it got without checking it. When the driver's memory is
exhausted the staging resource is NULL and the map dereferenced it.

Both allocations now fail the map, which the caller already handles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
index ff498778379705fda0032a475ef0c24fe8889e09..5821a7321b0d87600ea9ab8c59effe2fa40e9605 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -2814,6 +2814,8 @@ zink_buffer_map(struct pipe_context *pctx,
          if (usage & PIPE_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED) {
             trans->offset = box->x % MAX2(screen->info.props.limits.minMemoryMapAlignment, 1 << MIN_SLAB_ORDER);
             trans->staging_res = pipe_buffer_create(&screen->base, PIPE_BIND_LINEAR, PIPE_USAGE_STAGING, box->width + trans->offset);
+            if (!trans->staging_res)
+               goto fail;
             trans->unsync_upload = true;
          } else {
             /* If we are not called from the driver thread, we have
@@ -2828,6 +2830,8 @@ zink_buffer_map(struct pipe_context *pctx,
             u_upload_alloc_ref(mgr, 0, box->width,
                         screen->info.props.limits.minMemoryMapAlignment, &offset,
                         (struct pipe_resource **)&trans->staging_res, (void **)&ptr);
+            if (!trans->staging_res)
+               goto fail;
             trans->offset = offset;
          }
          res = zink_resource(trans->staging_res);
